From d4d18a87c41a2e0125c2fe70ae129ebcea0095d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Pires <bruno@blastersystems.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:04:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD=1 pads the fused KDA input stack to
 one eight-aligned width at TP=3 (upstream port)

Ported onto f350cd3 + patches 0001-0121 from upstream ashhart/TensorFold:
  96b3b7aa9 glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD keeps the fused KDA input stack packed at TP=3, split untouched
  316c0bc0f glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD - the prompt conv shift strides by the padded width too
  842bba3b6 glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD - the shared prompt window strides by the padded width
  6f7f99c21 glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD - the segment layout's row width is padded too
  831e20c12 glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD pads to ONE width for every rank
  b7af93459 glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD - the KDA input linear is packed at the padded width
  6bafb5aac glm cuda: KDA pad - one width for every layer and rank, MTP layer included
  9db24e79c glm cuda: the pad's comments are one line each (lean check)
  2d2a84fdf glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD pads a split KDA stack's bf16 rest too
  367e45011 glm cuda: glm-kda-pad-split's header is one line (lean check)
  c309bb354 glm cuda: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD read once into Settings, refused without glm_mm, the unpadded stack freed (review)

Opt-in, off by default, refused without TF_GLM_MM=1 (as upstream). A KDA layer's fused input stack is
3*heads*128 + 256 + heads columns. At TP=3 (22 / 21 / 21 heads) that is 8,726 / 8,341, not a multiple of eight, so
the stack, f_b and g_b are never tiled or packed (102 linears stay bf16 on tf_glm_bmm_decode) and f_b + g_b never
take the pair launch. With the pad every rank's stack carries one width, the widest rank's rounded up to eight
(8,728), its extra columns zero; heads stay 22 / 21 / 21. At TP=2 (12,576) and TP=4 (6,416) the width is already
aligned and the pad changes nothing. Upstream measured at TP=3 on three GB10s: 45.6 -> 56.7 tok/s at one stream,
KDA 15.0 -> 5.6 ms a forward.

Recipe-only changes beside the port:
- chainSegs (a shared decode window's KDA chains, recipe-only) passed p_stride = width(); cuda_shared copies each
  segment's projection rows into the state at the padded width, so with the pad the chains would read them at the
  wrong stride. Its Chain is now segChain(), which strides by matWidth(); cuda_kda_tp3_test checks it at every rank
  and world with the pad on and off, and that the padded TP=3 stack dispatches tiled with f_b + g_b in one launch.
- Settings and fingerprint layout 17 -> 18 (kda_pad); upstream's own layout number and its roce_multi, kv_host and
  solo fields are not taken.

The learn store's identity already separates padded from unpadded states: the padded State.proj sits inside each
rank's prefix, whose size goes into the identity's facts (and the probe hash differs with the packed weights).
